1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,440
Imagine asking for a video with one sentence:

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:08,912
explain my Cursor skills, in Swiss style,
five minutes, with bilingual subtitles.

3
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:11,580
You should not have to describe the fonts,

4
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:14,571
pacing, structure,
and export settings every time.

5
00:00:14,891 --> 00:00:20,459
A reusable skill stores those decisions,
so your next request can focus on the topic.

6
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:25,001
A skill is a recipe: when to use a workflow,

7
00:00:25,001 --> 00:00:28,398
what steps to follow,
and what a good result contains.

8
00:00:28,566 --> 00:00:32,683
Tools are equipment,
such as a video renderer or image generator.

9
00:00:33,003 --> 00:00:35,755
Cursor, Codex, and Claude Code are the cooks.

10
00:00:36,075 --> 00:00:40,577
Sharing a recipe does not automatically give
every cook the same equipment.

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,625
Your Mac already has a shared starting point.

12
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:46,532
Before this installation,

13
00:00:46,532 --> 00:00:50,341
the audit found eighty-three skill
folders under dot agents,

14
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:52,412
then skills, in your home folder.

15
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:56,578
Cursor separately maintained twenty-five skills
under dot cursor,

16
00:00:56,578 --> 00:00:58,021
then skills cursor.

17
00:00:58,071 --> 00:01:01,399
The ordinary dot cursor
skills folder did not exist.

18
00:01:01,719 --> 00:01:05,516
Similar names can describe very
different locations and owners.

19
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:10,792
Inside dot cursor,
extensions add editor features.

20
00:01:10,792 --> 00:01:15,288
Plugins bundle agent capabilities.
Projects stores working state,

21
00:01:15,288 --> 00:01:18,929
while the M C P configuration
names tool connections

22
00:01:18,929 --> 00:01:21,029
and hooks can launch commands.

23
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,336
Plugin caches can keep
several versions of one skill.

24
00:01:24,656 --> 00:01:27,835
A file's presence does not prove
the application loads it.

25
00:01:28,155 --> 00:01:31,632
The companion catalog
records all observed copies.

26
00:01:33,467 --> 00:01:36,882
Inside a skill folder,
find the skill markdown file.

27
00:01:36,882 --> 00:01:39,049
Its name and description identify

28
00:01:39,049 --> 00:01:42,555
when it applies.
The main text supplies the procedure.

29
00:01:42,734 --> 00:01:44,689
References hold style guidance,

30
00:01:44,689 --> 00:01:48,601
scripts automate rendering steps,
and assets supply templates.

31
00:01:48,921 --> 00:01:53,230
Together they turn a repeated conversation
into a reusable package.

32
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:56,942
Instructions still need tools
capable of carrying them out.

33
00:01:58,767 --> 00:02:01,241
To trace origin, distinguish the author,

34
00:02:01,241 --> 00:02:04,954
the software managing the files,
and whoever installed them.

35
00:02:05,134 --> 00:02:09,483
For example, twenty-six shared skill
files exactly match copies

36
00:02:09,483 --> 00:02:12,979
inside your Google Cloud Data Agent Kit
extension.

37
00:02:12,979 --> 00:02:15,006
That proves matching content.

38
00:02:15,006 --> 00:02:20,598
It does not prove who copied them.
Manifests and installer code provide evidence;

39
00:02:20,598 --> 00:02:23,843
timestamps alone cannot identify the installer.

40
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,768
Usefulness depends on the job.

41
00:02:27,768 --> 00:02:31,972
Bedrock and storage skills
can help with your A W S projects.

42
00:02:31,972 --> 00:02:36,452
Python dependency and notebook
skills support research workflows.

43
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:42,522
For videos, prioritize evidence, explanations,
visual design, narration, and rendering.

44
00:02:42,522 --> 00:02:45,449
Keep specialist skills for relevant topics.

45
00:02:45,449 --> 00:02:48,785
A large collection
is not automatically wasteful.

46
00:02:48,785 --> 00:02:53,005
Installed instructions
do not prove a connected service works.

47
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:56,183
For the new library,

48
00:02:56,183 --> 00:03:01,056
keep one editable source under your home
folder's dot agents skills directory.

49
00:03:01,376 --> 00:03:06,240
Current Cursor and Codex documentation
both recognize this location.

50
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:10,362
Claude Code gets a symbolic link
from its own skills folder,

51
00:03:10,362 --> 00:03:13,598
pointing to the same files.
Edit the source once.

52
00:03:13,598 --> 00:03:17,493
Keep application-managed skills and plugin
caches in place.

53
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:22,998
After installation,
check each application's skill picker.

54
00:03:22,998 --> 00:03:27,206
Select Conny Explainer Video
and first ask for a production brief.

55
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:30,649
Confirm that it uses
the intended preset and defaults.

56
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:35,055
Then test an override and a short render.
Can the app find the skill,

57
00:03:35,055 --> 00:03:40,421
follow its instructions, and produce the result?
Remote computers need their own setup.

58
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:45,738
The preset menu gives
your preferences short names:

59
00:03:45,738 --> 00:03:47,493
Swiss, cassette futurism,

60
00:03:47,493 --> 00:03:51,565
De Stijl, Bauhaus, NASA punk, Rhine Lab,
and pixel studio.

61
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:56,512
Your science-fiction references include
Starfield, NASA punk, and Rhine Lab.

62
00:03:56,832 --> 00:04:01,525
Each preset should specify palette,
typography, composition, and motion.

63
00:04:01,845 --> 00:04:06,560
A style name selects a design brief;
the rendered sample shows how well it works.

64
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:11,920
For this workflow,
the default brief is Swiss design,

65
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,713
five minutes, ten eighty p,

66
00:04:13,713 --> 00:04:18,960
thirty frames per second, English narration,
and Chinese plus English subtitles.

67
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,074
You only need to state changes.

68
00:04:21,394 --> 00:04:24,082
Asking for two minutes overrides the duration.

69
00:04:24,402 --> 00:04:27,627
The saved workflow should carry
your usual choices forward

70
00:04:27,627 --> 00:04:30,184
while keeping your current request in control.

71
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:33,596
For your next video, say:

72
00:04:33,596 --> 00:04:37,116
use Conny Explainer Video
to explain my Cursor skills,

73
00:04:37,116 --> 00:04:40,180
Swiss style, five minutes, bilingual subtitles.

74
00:04:40,334 --> 00:04:42,521
Our workflow separates three roles.

75
00:04:42,521 --> 00:04:45,770
The director checks the facts
and teaching sequence.

76
00:04:45,770 --> 00:04:48,426
The designer turns those ideas into frames.

77
00:04:48,426 --> 00:04:52,750
The engineer builds timing,
narration, captions, and the final render.

78
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:58,511
Review a sample, adjust the saved preferences,
and reuse the improved recipe next time.
